    },
    "message": "Start each parallel worker with one long simulation\n\npytest-xdist's worksteal scheduler hands each worker a contiguous block\nof the collected tests. The long_simulation tests sat in a few blocks,\nso one or two workers ran them back to back near the end while the\nothers had finished. A collection hook now puts one long simulation at\nthe head of each worker's block, so they all start at once.\n\nOn a 16-thread machine the full suite went from about 163 to 144\nseconds. Putting the long tests first instead gathered them on one\nworker (about 197 s), and --dist load rebuilt module fixtures on every\nworker (about 420 s). Runs without long simulations, or with one\nworker, keep their order.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
